    "type": "game",
    "name": "City Noodle Shop Simulator",
    "steam_appid": 2452010,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Operating a Chinese noodle restaurant</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The gameplay of this game involves running an ordinary noodle restaurant. You will play the role of the restaurant's operator, responsible for all aspects of the restaurant's operation and management, including recruiting staff, arranging tables, promoting the business, setting noodle prices, and more</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.poster.avif?t=1749169351\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.webm?t=1749169351\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.mp4?t=1749169351\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Strategic gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You need to consider factors such as the economic situation of the noodle shop, the number of staff, and customer preference levels. Based on the actual situation, you should customize strategies. Only by implementing the correct strategies can you better operate the noodle shop. Otherwise, you may incur losses or even go bankrupt </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Competitor's gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the game progresses to a certain stage, competitors will appear to disrupt your operations. You need to outperform your competitors in terms of weekly profits to make them retreat in the face of difficulties, thereby defeating them</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After defeating a certain number of competitors, you will reach the end of the game</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A collection of authentic noodle dishes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can learn the preparation of various noodles to enrich your menu. These noodles are mainly from China. Perhaps you have never heard of these noodles, but in the game, information about their origin and other aspects will be introduced. Perhaps while playing the game, you can increase your understanding of noodles from different regions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(Most of the noodle recipes in the game have been personally tasted by the authors who traveled to the local area for tasting)</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >There is more than one way to make money</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Is it better to pursue low profits but high sales volume, or to become an expensive yet exquisite noodle restaurant? Which method can make money? Actually, as long as the operation is reasonable, you can make money. You can completely build a profitable noodle restaurant based on your business philosophy</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Operating a Chinese noodle restaurant</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The gameplay of this game involves running an ordinary noodle restaurant. You will play the role of the restaurant's operator, responsible for all aspects of the restaurant's operation and management, including recruiting staff, arranging tables, promoting the business, setting noodle prices, and more</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.poster.avif?t=1749169351\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.webm?t=1749169351\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2452010/extras/aa80a2989bf9fd0cef2892966cacd9ac.mp4?t=1749169351\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Strategic gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You need to consider factors such as the economic situation of the noodle shop, the number of staff, and customer preference levels. Based on the actual situation, you should customize strategies. Only by implementing the correct strategies can you better operate the noodle shop. Otherwise, you may incur losses or even go bankrupt </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Competitor's gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the game progresses to a certain stage, competitors will appear to disrupt your operations. You need to outperform your competitors in terms of weekly profits to make them retreat in the face of difficulties, thereby defeating them</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After defeating a certain number of competitors, you will reach the end of the game</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A collection of authentic noodle dishes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can learn the preparation of various noodles to enrich your menu. These noodles are mainly from China. Perhaps you have never heard of these noodles, but in the game, information about their origin and other aspects will be introduced. Perhaps while playing the game, you can increase your understanding of noodles from different regions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(Most of the noodle recipes in the game have been personally tasted by the authors who traveled to the local area for tasting)</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >There is more than one way to make money</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Is it better to pursue low profits but high sales volume, or to become an expensive yet exquisite noodle restaurant? Which method can make money? Actually, as long as the operation is reasonable, you can make money. You can completely build a profitable noodle restaurant based on your business philosophy</p>",
    "short_description": "This is a strategy simulation game for Chinese noodle restaurant management. You will be responsible for formulating reasonable cost control and other strategies for the shop, ultimately enabling it to achieve profitability and defeat competitors",
